          %h3#Cohomology Cohomology – Twisted bivariant generalized geometric cohomology theory
          %p
            Where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categorical+hom-space"} (∞,1)-categorical hom-space
            in a general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            constitute a notion of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} tangent (∞,1)-topos
            specifically constitute
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+generalized+cohomology"} twisted generalized cohomology
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+bivariant+cohomology"} twisted bivariant cohomology
          %p
            For consider a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+object"} spectrum object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mo *
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \in T_\ast \mathbf{H}
            and write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi GL
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Grp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL_1(E) \in Grp(\mathbf{H})
            for its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group+of+units"} ∞-group of units
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-action"} ∞-action
            of this on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is (by the discussion there) exhibited by an object
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
