              for mapping into the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product"} dependent product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type-theoretic+axiom+of+choice"} type-theoretic axiom of choice
              again in the other direction. The resulting
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+space"} mapping space
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              to the claimed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+type"} function type
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E\to F)
              defined above. (See also
              = succeed ".)" do
                %a{:href => "http://nforum.mathforge.org/discussion/5321/parameterized-cohesive-spectra/?Focus=42394#Comment_42394"} this discussion
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              We have the following special cases of prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InternalHomGeneral"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mi a
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_a = 0
                  for all
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \colon A
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi B
                          %mo =
                          %mo *
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B = \ast
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⊢
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                          %mrow
                            %mi a
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                            %mi A
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\vdash \; \underset{a \colon A}{\prod} F
                %p
                  which reproduces the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+spectrum"} mapping spectrum
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi SpMap
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi Σ
                          %mn ∞
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SpMap(\Sigma^\infty A, F)
                  from prop.
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MappingSpectrumOutOfUnstableTypeAsCartesianInternalHom"}
              %li
                %p
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo =
                        %mi B
                        %mo =
                        %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = B = \ast
                  then the mapping type is
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi SpMap
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi E
                        %mo ,
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ⊢
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi Spectra
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\sigma \colon SpMap(E,F) \;\vdash \; F \colon Spectra
              %li
                %p
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mi a
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_a = 0
                  for all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \colon A
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi F
                          %mi b
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_b = 0
                  for all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \colon B
                  then the mapping type is
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi χ
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo →
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ⊢
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi Spectra
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\chi \colon (A \to B)\;\vdash \; 0 \colon Spectra
                        \\,.
          %h3#CohesiveAndDifferentialRefinement Cohesive and differential refinement
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T\mathbf{H}
            be a tangent cohesive
            = succeed "-topos" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mo *
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_\ast \mathbf{H}
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} stable (∞,1)-category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+objects"} spectrum objects
            inside it. We discuss how every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+type"} stable homotopy type
            here canonically sits in the middle of a
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology+diagram"} differential cohomology diagram
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              For every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mo *
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in T_\ast \mathbf{H}
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} naturality square
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mo ♭
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi pb
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Π
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi Π
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mo ♭
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}&amp; A/\flat A
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;{}^{(pb)}&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\Pi(A) &amp;\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \Pi(A/\flat A)
                    }
            %p
              (of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+modality"} shape modality
              applied to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+cofiber"} homotopy cofiber
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counit+of+a+comonad"} counit
              of the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+modality"} flat modality
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"} (∞,1)-pullback
              square.
          %p
            This was observed in (
            %a{:href => "#BunkeNikolausVoelkl13"}> Bunke-Nikolaus-Völkl 13
            ). It is an incarnation of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fracture+theorem"} fracture theorem
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              By
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} cohesion
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} stability
              we have the diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♭
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mo ♭
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Π
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo ♭
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi Π
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi Π
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mo ♭
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\flat A &amp;\longrightarrow &amp; A &amp;\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}&amp; A/\flat A
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\simeq}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\Pi(\flat A) &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \Pi(A) &amp;\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \Pi(A/\flat A)
                    }
            %p
              where both rows are
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber+sequences"} homotopy fiber sequences
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} cohesion
              the left vertical map is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} equivalence
              %a{:href => "homotopy+pullback#HomotopyFiberCharacterization"} homotopy fiber characterization
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullbacks"} homotopy pullbacks
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              This means that in stable cohesion every cohesive stable homotopy type is in controled sense a cohesive extension/refinement of its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization+of+cohesive+infinity-groupoids"} geometric realization
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+infinity-groupoid"} geometrically discrete
              (“bare”) stable
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
              by the non-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+object"} discrete
              part of its cohesive structure;
            %p
              In particular,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo ♭
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A/\flat A
              may be identified with differential cycle data. Indeed, by stability and cohesion it is the
              %a{:href => "cohesive+%28infinity,1%29-topos+--+structures#deRhamCohomology"} flat de Rham coefficient object
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo ♭
                    %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A/\flat A = \flat_{dR}\Sigma A
            %p
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension"} suspension
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maurer-Cartan+form"} Maurer-Cartan form
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi θ
                        %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta_A
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi θ
                                  %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ♭
                              %mi dR
                            %mi Σ
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi pb
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Π
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi Π
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mo ♭
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\stackrel{\theta_A}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \flat_{dR}\Sigma A
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;{}^{(pb)}&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\Pi(A) &amp;\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \Pi(A/\flat A)
                    }
            %p
              exhibits
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              as a
              = succeed "-coefficient" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+cohomology+theory"} generalized cohomology theory
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Π
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi(A)
            %p
              It follows by the discussion at
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
              that the further differential refinement
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{A}
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              should be given by a further
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi A
                              %mo ^
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Lie
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi pb
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi θ
                                  %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ♭
                              %mi dR
                            %mi Σ
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi pb
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Π
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi Π
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mo ♭
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\widehat{A} &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \Omega^1(-,Lie(A))
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;{}^{(pb)}&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    A &amp;\stackrel{\theta_A}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \flat_{dR}\Sigma A
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;{}^{(pb)}&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\Pi(A) &amp;\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \Pi(A/\flat A)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              But of course by the generality of the above proposition, such an
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{A}
              sits itself again in its fracture-like pullback diagram.
          %p Dually:
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              For every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mo *
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in T_\ast \mathbf{H}
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} naturality square
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♭
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi Π
                              %mi dR
                            %msup
                              %mi Σ
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn 1
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Π
                              %mi dR
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi Σ
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn 1
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♭
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\flat(\Pi_{dR} \Sigma^{-1} A) &amp;\longrightarrow &amp; \Pi_{dR}(\Sigma^{-1} A)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\flat A &amp;\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}&amp; A
                    }
            %p
              (of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+modality"} flat modality
              applied to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+a+monad"} unit
              of the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+modality"} shape modality
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"} (∞,1)-pullback
              square.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              As before but dually, the diagram extends to a morphism of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+cofiber"} homotopy cofiber
              diagrams of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♭
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi Π
                              %mi dR
                            %msup
                              %mi Σ
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn 1
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Π
                              %mi dR
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Ω
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♭
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♭
                            %mi Π
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mi Π
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\flat(\Pi_{dR} \Sigma^{-1} A) &amp;\longrightarrow &amp; \Pi_{dR}(\Omega A)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\flat A &amp;\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}&amp; A
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\flat \Pi(A) &amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \Pi(A)
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              and by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesion"} cohesion
              the bottom horizontal morphism is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} equivalence
          %p
            Combining these two statements yields the following (
            %a{:href => "#BunkeNikolausVoelkl13"}> Bunke-Nikolaus-Völkl 13
            ).
          #TheDifferentialDiagram.num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
              every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+type"} stable homotopy type
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Stab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi T
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in Stab(\mathbf{H}) \hookrightarrow T \mathbf{H}
              sits inside a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Π
                              %mi dR
                            %mi Ω
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ♭
                              %mi dR
                            %mi Σ
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi θ
                                    %mi A
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♭
                            %msub
                              %mi Π
                              %mi dR
                            %mi Ω
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi Π
                            %msub
                              %mo ♭
                              %mi dR
                            %mi Σ
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi Π
                                  %msub
                                    %mi θ
                                    %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♭
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi Π
                            %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp;  \Pi_{dR} \Omega A &amp;&amp; \longrightarrow &amp;&amp; \flat_{dR}\Sigma A
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \nearrow &amp; &amp; \searrow &amp; &amp; \nearrow_{\mathrlap{\theta_A}} &amp;&amp; \searrow
                    \\\
                    \\flat \Pi_{dR} \Omega A  &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; A &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; \Pi \flat_{dR}\Sigma A
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \searrow &amp;  &amp; \nearrow &amp; &amp; \searrow &amp;&amp; \nearrow_{\mathrlap{\Pi \theta_A}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \flat A &amp;&amp; \longrightarrow &amp;&amp; \Pi A
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              where the two squares are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
              squares and the two diagonals are the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+sequences"} fiber sequences
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maurer-Cartan+form"} Maurer-Cartan form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta_A
              and its dual.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              The bottom horizontal morphisms in the diagram in prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheDifferentialDiagram"}
              are the canonical
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "cohesive%20topos#CanonicalComparison"} points-to-pieces transform
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              This kind of diagram under forming
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0
              has been traditionally known from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
              and from
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+K-theory"} differential K-theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1208.3961"} Bunke 12, prop. 4.57
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology+diagram"} differential cohomology diagram
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
              of
              %em some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
              theory. This is a strong version of the synthetic notion “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"}> differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
              ” . For more on this see also at
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+spectrum"} smooth spectrum
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+of+spectra"} sheaf of spectra
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+spectrum"} smooth spectrum
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+generalized+cohomology"} twisted generalized cohomology
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+bivariant+cohomology"} twisted bivariant cohomology
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+differential+cohomology"} twisted differential cohomology
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+smooth+cohomology+in+string+theory"} twisted smooth cohomology in string theory
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The idea of forming
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mo *
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_\ast \mathbf{H}
            as a home for nontrivial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+types"} stable homotopy types
            was originally suggested by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Georg+Biedermann"} Georg Biedermann
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"} André Joyal
          %ul
            %li#Joyal08
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"}> André Joyal
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Notes on Logoi
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/IMA/JOYAL/Joyal.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            and see the further references at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} tangent (infinity,1)-topos
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mo *
                  %mi Smooth
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Stab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Smooth
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_\ast Smooth \infty Grpd \simeq Stab(Smooth \infty Grpd)
            is in
          %ul
            %li#BunkeNikolausVoelkl13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Bunke"}> Ulrich Bunke
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Nikolaus"} Thomas Nikolaus
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+V%C3%B6lkl"} Michael Völkl
              %em Differential cohomology theories as sheaves of spectra
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1311.3188"}> arXiv:1311.3188
              )
          %p
            For details see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology+hexagon"} differential cohomology hexagon
          %p
            The above discussion of geometric twisted generalized cohomology as cohomology in the tangent cohesive
            = succeed "-topos" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %ul
            %li#SchreiberTwists2013
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              , talk at
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://wwwmath.uni-muenster.de/sfb/sfb878/2013/twists.html"} Twists, generalised cohomology and applications
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "twisted+smooth+cohomology+in+string+theory#LocalPrequantumFieldTheory"} talk notes
          %p Discussion in a comprehensive context of cohesion is in section 4.2.3 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1310.7930"}> arXiv:1310.7930
              )
